WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.516
The operating system and runtime stack determine how easy the lab is

00:00:04.516 --> 00:00:07.092
to operate after the first successful demo.

00:00:07.092 --> 00:00:11.876
Windows can be convenient for desktop workflows, vendor tools, and mixed productivity use.

00:00:11.876 --> 00:00:15.924
Linux is common for server-style operation, containers, driver control, and automation.

00:00:15.924 --> 00:00:20.340
Some users choose dual boot or a dedicated lab system to keep

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:22.548
experiments away from a daily workstation.

00:00:22.548 --> 00:00:26.228
The best choice is the one you can maintain reliably.

00:00:26.228 --> 00:00:29.172
GPU drivers are a foundation, not an afterthought.

00:00:29.172 --> 00:00:32.852
Many AI runtimes depend on specific driver behavior, acceleration libraries,

00:00:32.852 --> 00:00:33.956
or container support.

00:00:33.956 --> 00:00:37.636
Once a stable configuration works, document it before changing versions.

00:00:37.636 --> 00:00:42.052
Driver updates can improve support, but they can also break a workflow.

00:00:42.052 --> 00:00:46.100
A lab should have an update discipline: know what is installed,

00:00:46.100 --> 00:00:47.572
why it is installed,

00:00:47.572 --> 00:00:52.356
and how you would return to a working state if an upgrade fails.

00:00:52.356 --> 00:00:55.668
The runtime stack may include container runtimes, Python environments,

00:00:55.668 --> 00:00:59.348
local inference runtimes, model managers, web frontends, notebooks, and APIs.

00:00:59.348 --> 00:01:01.924
These components change quickly, so separation matters.

00:01:01.924 --> 00:01:06.340
Keep the base system stable while experiments change in containers, virtual environments,

00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:07.444
or dedicated directories.

00:01:07.444 --> 00:01:12.964
Avoid letting every tool install global dependencies until the machine becomes impossible to reason about.

00:01:12.964 --> 00:01:15.172
Documentation is a practical reliability control.

00:01:15.172 --> 00:01:18.484
Record installation commands, driver versions, model locations, service ports,

00:01:18.484 --> 00:01:20.324
environment variables, and configuration files.

00:01:20.324 --> 00:01:23.636
This does not need to be formal enterprise documentation.

00:01:23.636 --> 00:01:28.420
A simple lab notebook can save hours when you rebuild, troubleshoot, compare performance,

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:30.260
or explain your setup later.

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:35.780
A homelab becomes more valuable when the environment can be recreated instead of merely remembered.
